# ProsperMinds main site (prosper-minds.com) — environment configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in the real values:
#     cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and is blocked from the web by the dotfile rule in
# .htaccess. To keep it outside the document root entirely, put it anywhere
# readable by PHP and set PM_ENV_FILE to its absolute path in the server
# environment.
#
# Anything set as a real server environment variable (cPanel "Environment
# Variables", or SetEnv in the vhost) wins over this file.
#
# NOTE: the CPD subdomain uses the SAME variable names with DIFFERENT values.
# The two sites must not share one .env file.
#
# Parsing is literal: everything after the first "=" is the value. There is no
# inline-comment stripping and no $VAR interpolation, so passwords containing
# # $ { } & etc. can be pasted verbatim. Wrap in single quotes if the value has
# leading or trailing spaces.

# ── Database (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_USER, DB_PASS and DB_NAME have no fallback. If they are missing, every
# page returns "Site configuration is incomplete."
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=3306
DB_NAME=replace_with_database_name
DB_USER=replace_with_database_user
DB_PASS=replace_with_database_password

# ── SMTP (OPTIONAL) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these commented out in production. When unset, the site keeps reading
# SMTP settings from the `site_settings` table exactly as it does today, so the
# admin UI stays in charge of them.
#
# Set them to force all outbound mail somewhere else — a local mail-catcher
# during development, or to move the SMTP password out of the database and into
# the server environment.
#
# SMTP_SECURE accepts: tls (STARTTLS), ssl (implicit TLS), or none.
#
# Local development against the Mailpit container from docker-compose.yml:
#   SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   SMTP_PORT=1025
#   SMTP_SECURE=none
#   SMTP_USER=local@example.test
#   SMTP_PASS=anything-mailpit-accepts-any
#   SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=local@example.test
#
#SMTP_HOST=
#SMTP_PORT=
#SMTP_SECURE=
#SMTP_USER=
#SMTP_PASS=
#SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=

# Local development only, for the reCAPTCHA and "let blocked people through"
# tests. Leave all three unset on the live site.
#
# Where the site asks "is this token a person?". Defaults to Google. The test
# suite points it at local-dev/recaptcha-stub (php -S 127.0.0.1:8083).
#PM_RECAPTCHA_VERIFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8083/siteverify
#
# Extra host names a token may have been issued for (comma separated).
#PM_RECAPTCHA_ALLOW_HOST=
#
# Where the server sends the request that replays a blocked form. Defaults to
# the site's own address; locally the page is on http://127.0.0.1:8080.
#PM_LOOPBACK_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8080
